# Component Rules

## Structure
```tsx
// 1. Imports (type imports first)
import type { ComponentProps } from "react";
import { useState } from "react";

// 2. Types
interface ButtonProps extends ComponentProps<"button"> {
  variant: "primary" | "secondary";
}

// 3. Component (named export)
export function Button({ variant, children, ...props }: ButtonProps) {
  return (
    <button data-variant={variant} {...props}>
      {children}
    </button>
  );
}
```

## Rules
- Always name the export to match filename: `Button.tsx` → `export function Button`
- Props interface: `<ComponentName>Props`
- No inline object styles — use CSS modules or utility classes
- Keyboard accessibility required for interactive elements
